<title>RUSSIA: Russia launches &quot;hot-line&quot; communication satellite.</title>
<headline>Russia launches &quot;hot-line&quot; communication satellite.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia on Thursday launched a special communications satellite which will help provide an improved &quot;hot-line&quot; link between the presidents of Russia and the United States, a space official said.</p>
<p>A spokesman for the Military Space Forces' headquarters said a rocket bearing the Molniya-3 satellite blasted off at 3.37 p.m (1137 GMT) from the Plesetsk cosmodrome in northern Russia.</p>
<p>The satellite, designed to orbit the earth at an altitude of 41,000 km (25,500 miles), will replace an earlier outdated Molniya probe which provides long-range telephone communications and transmits radio and television programmes around Russia.</p>
<p>The satellite will also carry one of the many special telecommunications channels which go to make up the &quot;hot line&quot; which links the White House and the Kremlin.</p>
</text>
